  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1... \n\nFreezing conditions are expected across much of the CWA this \nmorning, as sky cover gradually clears, and winds remain light to \ncalm, as high pressure nudges into the area from the west. This will \nset up a period of dry conditions through at least early next week, \nalong with a gradual warming trend, particularly by Tuesday as \nsoutherly flow increases out ahead of an approaching system. \n\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2...\n\nBy Wednesday into Thursday, a potent upper level trough and \nassociated cold front will approach the area. Precipitation will \nstart out as rain across the area, and could be moderate in \nintensity at times. Precipitation will gradually transition over to \nsnow, or a rain snow mix at times, as a deep upper trough forms \nacross the eastern U.S., ushering in much colder and blustery \nconditions. At least minor accumulations are possible across the \nmountains, as a prolonged period of northwesterly upslope flow takes \nhold.",
